# Raiding Schemes: two of them give a noncreature spell two instances of conspire, each paid separately and each triggering on
# its own payment alone (CR 702.78b, the card's ruling), each with creatures of its own (CR 118.3). Bot1 casts four green
# creatures on turn 1 and a Raiding Schemes on turns 3 and 5 (the second Schemes, a noncreature spell, has conspire from the
# first: declined). On turn 7 Giant Growth on Avacyn's Pilgrim declines the first conspire and pays the second, tapping Llanowar
# Elves and Elvish Mystic: one trigger, one copy, kept on the Pilgrim, which is 7/7. On turn 9 a second Giant Growth pays both:
# the first taps Llanowar Elves and Elvish Mystic, the second may not choose either again (! Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)) and
# taps Noble Hierarch and the Pilgrim: two triggers, two copies, the Pilgrim 10/10.

